// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PrisonerOrders 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4205102459" "Nemesis Army Prisoner Protocols"
// DetailString :
"P1842489435" "You recovered these orders from Nemesis Army soldiers working in the Shadow Shard. They tell all Nemesis Army soldiers to make an effort to capture human Shadow Shard natives, and take them to a specified location for interrogation."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NemesisPortals 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P714142975" "Further interrogations"
// DetailString :
"P2580168577" "These orders pick out specific prisoners to transfer back to Paragon City. There's enough information here to find the the base where these people are being held. <br><br>From the sound of things, it would appear that the Nemesis Army has developed portals of their own to move men and material back and forth between Paragon and the Shadow Shard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - OldFred 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P828849374" "The words of Old Fred"
// DetailString :
"P257769653" "After you rescued him from the Nemesis Army, the native called Old Fred told you: <br><br>'They caught us all, and more before to learn about the Legend of Ruladak the Strong. It's best that they don't know. It's best that nobody knows anymore.  <br><br>I thank you for my freedom, but don't look to me for answers and I won't tell you nothing that no one should hear."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LegendOfRuladak 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P792196903" "A native myth"
// DetailString :
"P1422037831" "After rescuing a second group of captives taken by the Nemesis Army to learn about the legend of Ruladak the Strong, Sara Moore told you: <br><br>'The Legend of Ruladak is about a monster that controls the Rularuu. We tell it ever since the madness broke the world, to remind us that we have to help each other to survive. <br><br>The legend goes that when the madness broke the world, there was a time when kindness walked the land and all were hopeful. But then Ruladak the Strong appeared. He was angry because the People of Paragon had turned away from the Rularuu, and so he sought to slay the people of Paragon to punish them. Fearing for the people, all the kindness in the world gathered itself together and tried to destroy Ruladak and the Rularuu. The battle lasted for days and broke the very islands, but in the end there was only enough kindness to force Ruladak into a deep slumber. He still guides the Rularuu even in his sleep, but as long as kindness remains strong in the hearts of the People of Paragon, Ruladak will never awaken and we will be spared. <br><br>I know it must sound foolish to great heroes like you, but it's just a story for children. Though, I used to think that the Prince of Brass was just a story, too.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NewPortals 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1666547397" "Dimensional Transit Orders"
// DetailString :
"P1243293133" "These orders form a schedule of upcoming dimensional tranits from Paragon City to the Shadow Shard and back for the Nemesis Army. This schedule could help intercept Nemesis Army groups before they can establish themselves in the Shadow Shard, but it also clearly shows that they have built dimensional portals of their own."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Awakening 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1547707316" "A half-finished letter"
// DetailString :
"P2167525633" "This unfinished letter is written from a Captian Easting of the Nemesis Army to a General Fort, apparently his commander. The letter expresses Cpt. Easting's concerns about the operation he's been assigned to. There are several different drafts of it on the same piece of paper, all written by the same hand. One particular section stands out to you: <br><br>'I am uncertain if the Nemesis Army High Command would approve of your decision to advance to the next phase of the operation. The very fact that the Circle of Thorns has begun to act should surely be a warning. What if they are right? If we can awaken this creature, are you certain it would act as an ally? Of all the native legends we've gathered, there are none where a bargain has ever been struck with the Rularuu or their commander."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - OldFred2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1153145628" "Old Fred's book"
// DetailString :
"P1481781305" "After rescueing him from the Circle of Thorns, Old Fred told you: <br><br>'The Nemesis Army didn't know at first, but I did. I was just old enough when the madness broke the world. How long ago was it? 15 years? 20? There's no sun, nor moon, nor seasons here. And even I only know those things from stories. <br><br>When the madness came, I was just old enough to remember the days afterwards. The Kind One promised us a new age, free from Rularuu, where we could grow and live in peace. But then we found out that when the world had been broken, Ruladak had been trapped in this part of it. Ruladak is real. I saw him once, when my eyes were young. Tyrannous and strong, my mother called him, but his creatures snuffed out her life too. <br><br>Living here, hunted by the Rularuu, few remain who saw it all. Mostly just children of the survivors. But my father, he wrote a book. It told all about how the Kind one bound Ruladak, and how the seal could be re-made. I came back to find it, to help Sara and you all. But they took it. They took it away in a demon's hand, took it back to their ancient city of the dead.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Legendbook 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1922236615" "The Story of Ruladak"
// DetailString :
"P2827317171" "This handwritten journal is filled by page upon page of densley-cramped writing. Part-way between a journal, a survival guide, and story book, it talks a great deal about living and surviving in the Shadow Shard. <br><br>The first entries in the book start with talk of a great cataclysm, when 'The Mad One broke the world'. It speaks next about the short golden age that followed, when 'The Kind One' traveled the lands, promising the survivors that salvation was close at hand, and that their oaths to Rularuu were no more. No mention is made of what the oaths to Rularuu were. <br><br>The next set of events deals with the appearance of Ruladak the Strong. Ruladak is called the Brother to Kindness and Brother to Madness, and is called the 'Iron Fist of Rularuu'. The book describes battles between Ruladak, the 'Mad One', and the 'Kind One'. Finally, it details how the Kind One sealed Ruladak away with 4 mystic seals."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WhispInterrogations 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2538334713" "Interrogations by the Rularuu"
// DetailString :
"P2140962500" "You rescued several Shadow Shard natives who were captured and interrogated by the Rularuu. The creatures seemed intent on learning more about the Nemesis Army. More disturbing is that they claimed to be gathering information for Ruladak the Strong."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Treaty 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2157775680" "A Traitor's Treaty"
// DetailString :
"P3962384919" "These documents comprise a treaty signed by a General Fort and a representative of Ruladak the Strong. It is marked as one copy of several. The terms are straight-forward, but have huge implications. In exchange for the Nemesis Army freeing it from it's imprisonment, Ruladak the Strong promises to aid General Fort in an attempt to take control of the Nemesis Army from it's high command. <br><br>The treaty specifies how to break Ruladak from confinement in a step-by step manner. With this information, Ruladak will not be imprisoned for long."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - 4thSealLoc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2873678135" "Crucial information"
// DetailString :
"P1316977929" "After a battle, one of the Nemesis troops you questioned told you: <br><br>'That seal thing that everyone is looking for? I know where it is. General Fort wanted to use it to force a better bargain on this Ruladak creature. He has it with him in a base in the Marooned Shores. <br><br>General Fort is a fool to think he'll succeed anyway. I joined the Nemesis Army to serve the glory of Lord Nemesis. General Fort is just a power-hungry mad-man. Nemesis, he's the new Prometheus, he's a new deity. He's the master I serve, not some jumped-up general."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FortsWords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4181525728" "The defeat of General Fort"
// DetailString :
"P3335287882" "After his defeat, General Fort had some final words for you: <br><br>'I was a fool. I was used. Ruladak promised me such power, power enough to stand against Nemesis and take the Army for my own. I didn't see the monster's own motives, though. I thought it a sleeping beast, a great stupid monster I could harness and ride to victory. Now I see that I was the one led on a leash. It is already awakened. It will soon be rousing. It will soon be free. Then, heaven help you all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2184349531" "The Legend of Ruladak"
// DetailString :
"P1804087960" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2012317414" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P187499789" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4099866668" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P345018226" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode6Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1057201799" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode7Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3963508373" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode8Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4212187590" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode9Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3187294756" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode10Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4255845382" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned. <br><br>You secured the second seal, which could be used by trained mystics to weaken Ruladak should he awaken."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode11Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1621437822" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned. <br><br>You secured the second seal, which could be used by trained mystics to weaken Ruladak should he awaken. <br><br>You were also able to secure the third seal, which kept Ruladak from fully re-connecting with the Rularuu."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode12Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4152708566" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned. <br><br>You secured the second seal, which could be used by trained mystics to weaken Ruladak should he awaken. <br><br>You were also able to secure the third seal, which kept Ruladak from fully re-connecting with the Rularuu. <br><br>You went after the last seal, only to find it missing."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode13Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1958476648" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned. <br><br>You secured the second seal, which could be used by trained mystics to weaken Ruladak should he awaken. <br><br>You were also able to secure the third seal, which kept Ruladak from fully re-connecting with the Rularuu. <br><br>You went after the last seal, only to find it missing. <br><br>You then battled the Nemesis Army to find the location of the 4th seal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode14Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3114231024" "Sara Moore asked you to find out if the Nemesis Army really was kidnapping Shard natives. You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned. <br><br>You secured the second seal, which could be used by trained mystics to weaken Ruladak should he awaken. <br><br>You were also able to secure the third seal, which kept Ruladak from fully re-connecting with the Rularuu. <br><br>You went after the last seal, only to find it missing. <br><br>You then battled the Nemesis Army to find the location of the 4th seal. <br><br>You recovered the seal and defeated General Fort, only to learn that Fort had been used and that Ruladak the Strong was already about to awaken."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL8_TaskForceMoore_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P112612045" "When Sara Moore asked for your help to find out who had been kidnapping natives, you couldn't have known that it would lead you to uncover <br><br>The Legend of Ruladak <br><br> You fought Nemesis Army troops around the Cascade Archipelago, and found that they were under order to do just that. <br><br>You then rescued several natives who had been captured by the Nemesis Army, who were interrogating them to find out about a native legend about a monster called 'Ruladak'. <br><br>You liberated more captives from the Nemesis Army who were also being interrogated about the myths of Ruladak, including a man called 'Old Fred' who seemed to know more than he was telling. On your return, Sara Moore told you the myth of Ruladak, about a monster that tried to force the natives to worship the Rularuu after 'the madness broke the world', but was imprisoned by kindness. <br><br>You next struck a Nemesis Army base, and recovered a letter to a 'General Fort' of the Nemesis army, talking about plans to awaken some sleeping power and ally with the Rularuu. <br><br>You next learned that Old Fred, one of the oldest and wisest of the people in the Shadow Shard, had been kidnapped by the Circle of Thorns when he was looking for a book written by his father about Ruladak. You rescued him, and he told you that Ruladak was real! The Circle, however, had already taken the book back to Oranbega. <br><br>You returned to Paragon City and recovered the book from Oranbega. It detailed a great deal of information about how Ruladak the Strong had been bound by the 'Kind One'. <br><br>While the book was off being analyzed, you went looking for another group of natives who had been kidnapped. You found that they had actually been taken by the Rularuu, who were interrogating the natives for what they knew of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>The worst came to pass when you attacked a Nemesis base and found that a Nemesis Army leader named General Fort had signed a treaty with the Rularuu to free Ruladak and ally with the creature in an attempt to sieze control of the Nemesis Army. <br><br>You began the battle to stop the Nemesis Army from awakening Ruladak the Strong. The Nemesis Army had already gotten to the first of the 4 seals that held Ruladak imprisoned. <br><br>You secured the second seal, which could be used by trained mystics to weaken Ruladak should he awaken. <br><br>You were also able to secure the third seal, which kept Ruladak from fully re-connecting with the Rularuu. <br><br>You went after the last seal, only to find it missing. <br><br>You then battled the Nemesis Army to find the location of the 4th seal. <br><br>You recovered the seal and defeated General Fort, only to learn that Fort had been used and that Ruladak the Strong was already about to awaken. <br><br>You entered deep into his lair and battled Ruladak the Strong. Sara Moore could hardly contain herself, as she had just seen mythic heroes write the end chapter of the Legend of Ruladak."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_TFM_KillTask1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P89025791" "The People of Paragon have been able to live healthily even here thanks to the Kora fruit. It keeps us healthy and helps us stay well despite the hardships we face. Parties of Kora gatherers have recently come under attack by strangers, and some have been kidnapped. Our own searchers have found no trace, and the scouts of the General are spread too thin watching for the Rularuu. Thus, I ask you to help find our missing people."
// AcceptString :
"P2214354495" "Help find missing natives"
// SendOffString :
"P3434923004" "Those that escaped capture said that the attackers looked like Brasswork Devils, so at first we thought they were Reflections from the Rularuu. However, they captured instead of killed, and so could not be of the Rularuu. I think that they may be actual Brasswork Devils, servants of the Prince of Brass. We had thought them just myths of our forefathers from before the Madness broke the world, conjured by Reflections to terrify us, but Lieutenant Colonel Flynn says that they are real, and are called the Nemesis Army. If it is truly them, then those captured may still be alive, and these soldiers of the Nemesis Army may have information to find the missing. <br><br>I charge you to confront this Nemesis Army here within the Cascades, and take the truth from them by force!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3660607349" "Defeat Nemesis Army for info"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2792198294" "You must confront the Nemesis Army in the Cascades and take the truth of what has happened to the people they have captured."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2191044836" "You captured orders from one of the defeated Nemesis Army soldiers"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3593318416" "The orders you found are proof without doubt! The machine-hearted devils of the Prince of Brass are surely the culprits! I will get Lieutenant Colonel Flynn's help to find where the Nemesis are keeping my people, and then with your strength they can be rescued."
// RandomFameString :
"P2683765818" "The refugees from the Shadow Shard have been talking about {TaskForceName} a lot."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_TFM_Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3616740940" "Your bravery has helped us greatly, and now we know where the Brass-hearted devils of the Nemesis have taken their captives. They have built a base within the shard to experiment and interrogate, but thanks to you we have found it."
// AcceptString :
"P4135743864" "Rescue captives from Nemesis"
// SendOffString :
"P3687833770" "We have found the location where the people are being held, and now you must give them freedom. You must also defeat the leader of this nest of Devils, to show them the fate of those who would poison or destroy the Peoples of Paragon."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2519642204" "Defeat Nemesis base leaders"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1160194691" "You must give freedom to the captive people held by the Nemesis. You must also defeat the leader of this nest of Devils, to show them the fate of those who would poison or destroy the Peoples of Paragon."

